   "summary": "Despatch No. 4611 transmits Report No. 161 surveying political, diplomatic, and economic developments in Japan during February 1940. The report details acute Japanese apprehensions over potential American economic embargoes and naval expansion following the expiration of the 1911 commercial treaty, as well as parliamentary debates over the Nine-Power Treaty and outstanding American claims in China. It records the diplomatic compromise settling the Asama Maru affair with Great Britain, major military advances and subsequent withdrawals in Suiyuan and Kwangsi, continuing strikes against the Haiphong-Yunnan Railway, and preparations for establishing Wang Ching-wei's government at Nanking. Internally, the report focuses on the reconvening of the Diet, the political storm resulting from Takao Saito's critical interpellation on the China war, ongoing coal and hydroelectric shortages curtailing Kansai industries, and emerging national rice deficits prompting massive grain purchases abroad.",
